WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:05.180
Your boss’ office, his name etched onto
the frosted-glass window in the door, sitting

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.589
at the end of a long hallway.

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:11.440
He called you in, and you don’t know if
you’ll be leaving with your job.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.650
A grimy public bathroom filled with graffiti,
spiders, cracked toilet seats, and a sinister

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.020
shadow in the very last stall.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:25.830
A surgical theatre, where masked doctors wait
with gleaming scalpels, forceps, and bone

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:30.320
saws, preparing for an operation that you
don’t know if you’ll wake up from.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.840
All of these have one thing in common: They’re
rooms that inspire dread.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:41.010
But after this video, you’ll look back on
all of them like you would your cozy childhood

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.010
bedroom.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.090
A wise man once said, “Life has many doors.”

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:50.340
What he didn’t say is that sometimes, opening
the wrong door can be a way of bringing that

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.000
life to an untimely end, or worse.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.610
Especially when you’re dealing with the
kind of horrifying anomalies secured and contained

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.760
by the SCP Foundation.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.850
You may think it’s what’s lurking inside
the room that might be your biggest threat,

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.750
but that’s a potentially lethal assumption.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.210
Sometimes, the most dangerous thing is the
room itself.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:16.730
And that’s what we’re here to talk about
today: Seven of the most terrifying rooms

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:22.780
on the Foundation’s database, none of which
have ever been featured on this channel before.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:26.700
So reach out, grab the handle, and open the
door.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.750
Welcome to the SCP Foundation’s most terrifying
rooms.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.800
All you can do is hope that, by the end, you’ll
actually be able to leave.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:43.040
We’ll begin with an old classic from Series
One: SCP-002, a maleficent meatball known

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.930
as The “Living” Room.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:48.979
There’s a decent chance you’re sitting
in your living room right now while you watch

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:53.700
this video, so you may be thinking, “What’s
so wrong about that?”

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:59.760
But this really is a living room, and it’s
always on the lookout for some tasteful new

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:00.760
furniture.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:06.780
From the outside, SCP-002 appears to be a
huge, tumorous blob made out of living flesh.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.410
Sure, that may seem off-putting, but don’t
be so superficial.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:14.860
The inside of 002 is a different story.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:19.450
It may appear like your standard low-rent
apartment from within, but this place has

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.280
a lot of personality.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.950
There’s a single window, despite there being
no opening for a window from the outside.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:32.010
In addition to all the standard furniture
- chairs, tables, a TV stand - it’s actually

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:37.590
developed a number of other wonderful amenities
since being contained by the Foundation, including

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:44.310
two lamps, a throw rug, a television, a radio,
a beanbag chair, three books in an unknown

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:48.459
language, four children's toys, and a small
potted plant.

00:02:48.459 --> 00:02:51.959
The first thing you might notice about the
room is the funny smell.

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:56.080
Then, you might take a closer look at all
that lovely furniture.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:01.280
That’s when you’ll realize that every
single piece of furniture in there is made

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:07.349
out of human tissue - wood is polished and
varnished bone, fabrics are woven from human

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:11.239
hair, leather is made from tanned human skin.

00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:16.250
This is what happens to anyone who enters
SCP-002.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:20.940
And sadly, if you’ve gotten close enough
to see this, it’s already too late.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:26.160
We hope you enjoy the rest of your existence...as
a brand new armchair.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.030
But maybe you don’t want to get turned into
furniture inside a living room within a giant

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.030
tumor.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:39.030
Maybe you’ve got more specific needs: You
like puzzles, exercises, and most of all,

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.030
solitude.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:44.720
You like to test your mental and physical
fortitude, without worrying about the distractions

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.920
caused by having to deal with other human
beings.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.390
If that sounds like you, then let’s get
your feet wet and tell you about a wonderful

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:58.849
piece of prime real estate you can find Under
the Sea: SCP-057.

00:03:58.849 --> 00:04:04.519
This underwater chamber is almost impossible
to get to without a James Cameron-style mini-submarine,

00:04:04.519 --> 00:04:07.040
but believe us, it’s worth the effort.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:12.599
If you manage to access SCP-057 and enter
its submerged chamber, then you’re going

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:16.250
to be treated to the best, last challenge
of your life.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:22.909
The door will close behind you, permanently,
ensuring that wonderful privacy you so covet.

00:04:22.909 --> 00:04:29.900
Then, the walls - these impenetrable monoliths
of slate-covered stone - will begin to move.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:34.969
Like a kind of high-stakes game show, you’ll
need to keep moving, avoiding the ever-shifting

00:04:34.969 --> 00:04:39.770
walls as the environment around you becomes
more and more disorienting.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:45.999
There is no escape, only survival - and survival
is only temporary.

00:04:45.999 --> 00:04:51.030
When your body fails you, or your mind snaps
under the weight of sustained mortal terror,

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.930
that’s when those walls will close in.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:05:02.309
The monoliths of SCP-057 will get closer,
and closer, and closer...until your body is

00:05:02.309 --> 00:05:08.939
crushed between them, killing you with a torturously
slow squeeze where nothing and nobody will

00:05:08.939 --> 00:05:12.279
ever hear your final choked screams.

00:05:12.279 --> 00:05:16.069
But it’s all worth it for that glorious
ocean view!

00:05:16.069 --> 00:05:18.690
Look at all those adorable little fishies!

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:21.939
But hey, maybe seapunk isn’t your favorite
aesthetic.

00:05:21.939 --> 00:05:24.520
Maybe you’re the more industrial type.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:28.509
You couldn’t feel more at home than among
a complex network of anomalous pipes.

00:05:28.509 --> 00:05:34.949
We’ll admit, that’s eerily specific, but
it isn’t half as eerie as SCP-015.

00:05:34.949 --> 00:05:39.919
If ever you find yourself opening the door
to the main room of a certain undisclosed

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:45.389
warehouse, you’ll feel like you’ve walked
into an early 2000s screensaver with a decidedly

00:05:45.389 --> 00:05:51.879
gritty edge: An impossibly huge and intricate
mass of pipes, vents, boilers, and other various

00:05:51.879 --> 00:05:58.249
plumbing apparatus, that just keeps growing,
seemingly becoming more strange and anomalous

00:05:58.249 --> 00:05:59.789
as it does so.

00:05:59.789 --> 00:06:05.900
These pipes have been made out of bone, wood,
steel, pressed ash, human flesh, glass, and

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:06.900
granite.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:11.800
There aren’t any pipes made out of traditional
pipe-making materials, like lead, copper,

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.840
ceramics, or PVC.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:17.699
And if you think what the pipes are made of
is weird, the materials that travel through

00:06:17.699 --> 00:06:19.669
them are even freakier.

00:06:19.669 --> 00:06:26.219
These include oil, mercury, rats, a species
of insect not yet identified, ground glass,

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:29.629
seawater, entrails, and molten iron.

00:06:29.629 --> 00:06:34.830
And this is important to remember because
if you appear hostile to SCP-015, or enter

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:39.830
the room carrying tools, the pipes will begin
to burst and spray you with their contents

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.599
in self-defense.

00:06:41.599 --> 00:06:45.559
Resulting in one of the few times in human
history where you’d be incredibly lucky

00:06:45.559 --> 00:06:49.250
to only be sprayed with rats or human entrails.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:54.599
Much like SCP-173, the Sculpture, it’s important
to keep this room under strict observation.

00:06:54.599 --> 00:07:00.240
It’s when the pipes are left unoccupied
that they start expanding, and trying to grow

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:04.389
downwards, in hopes of mixing with the sewer
system below.

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:09.520
If ever that happens, then the pipes may end
up coming to a room near you.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:14.759
And considering that people have also reported
screaming coming from inside the pipes, what

00:07:14.759 --> 00:07:20.199
comes out of them may not even be as frightening
as what could be going in...

00:07:20.199 --> 00:07:22.729
But maybe you don’t want a warehouse.

00:07:22.729 --> 00:07:27.159
Perhaps you just want to rent a small, cozy
room in a one-story building over in Weehawken,

00:07:27.159 --> 00:07:28.369
New Jersey.

00:07:28.369 --> 00:07:35.649
Problem is, if you try to do this, you might
end up lodging in SCP-5256, a room that defies

00:07:35.649 --> 00:07:42.249
reality in a number of freaky ways thanks
to its prior occupant: A highly unstable reality

00:07:42.249 --> 00:07:43.249
warper.

00:07:43.249 --> 00:07:47.650
The reality filters get stronger the further
you go into the room, with the terminus being

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:52.369
the room’s far corner, which presents as
an empty void that’s impossible to even

00:07:52.369 --> 00:07:53.369
see.

00:07:53.369 --> 00:07:56.400
A damaged bloody hammer is lodged into the
far wall.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:00.249
Metal fragments covered in human blood float
near the entrance.

00:08:00.249 --> 00:08:02.639
Half-eaten bugs all over the floor.

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:07.360
There’s a crucifix on the wall, along with
medical-grade anesthetics with trace amounts

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.569
of neural tissue inside.

00:08:09.569 --> 00:08:14.819
All evidence points to the reality warper
having been the victim of atrocious and inhumane

00:08:14.819 --> 00:08:19.490
acts, perhaps as a way to “cure” it of
its anomalous affliction.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:25.979
And to add to the creep factor, many believe
its body is still there, lurking in the unseeable

00:08:25.979 --> 00:08:26.979
corner.

00:08:26.979 --> 00:08:28.119
How do we know?

00:08:28.119 --> 00:08:32.680
Because despite the corner of the room being
unseeable, people have still performed simple

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:36.640
tactile tests by sticking their hands into
the space.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:41.521
One D-Class reported it feeling like leathery
flesh with occasional scraps of fabric, and

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:45.310
sharp needle-like objects occasionally sticking
out of its skin.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:48.570
But for rent this cheap, who can really complain
about a body or two?

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:53.190
But that’s enough about things that are
just creepy, let’s get dangerous instead.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:57.590
A room that won’t just freak you out with
some eerie anomalous sights.

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:01.210
If you get unlucky, it’ll give you a horrifying
death.

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.970
After all, who doesn’t like a little excitement?

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:11.260
Step into SCP-4595, a small room in a woodshed
behind an abandoned house near Jasper, Indiana.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:14.140
You’ll be taken in by its rustic charm at
first.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:18.200
It’s a quiet, peaceful setting, where you’re
alone with your thoughts.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:22.820
When the room was first found, it contained
a small, bloodstained shovel and the skeleton

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.570
of an adolescent male.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:26.010
But don’t let that put you off.

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:29.930
Don’t let the charcoal marking of the word
“WITCH” written on the exterior door bother

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:30.930
you either.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:33.610
It all just adds to the character of the room.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:41.130
Oh, though there’s one thing we should probably
mention: There is an entity, known as SCP-4595-A,

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.650
that lives a meter beneath the room.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:49.110
She’s a witch-like creature, rotted and
covered in wounds on her torso and face.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:53.460
Her mere presence will instill a sense of
paranoia and dread into you, getting worse

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.970
and worse the longer you’re in there.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:57.630
But stay quiet about it.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:03.700
If at any point, you disturb SCP-4595, all
the empty spaces in your chest cavity, as

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:09.410
well as your lungs, airways, stomach, and
intestine, will suddenly fill with live desert

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:13.870
locusts, causing you to experience a horrible
death.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:16.400
So be a considerate upstairs neighbor.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.400
Or else.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:22.100
So, remember when we said earlier that it’s
not always what’s inside the room that can

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.450
cause you harm?

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:27.260
Sometimes, it’s the thing right on the other
side of the door.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:29.270
Look at the nearest closed door.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.800
Really focus on it.

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:35.830
Tell us, how can you be so sure there’s
not something on the other side?

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:38.970
Can’t you hear its heavy, wheezing breaths?

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:48.110
It’s not a home invader, it’s something
even worse: SCP-303, and it can make any room,

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:52.020
anywhere, an absolute nightmare for you.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.600
Keep an eye on that door while we explain.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:11:02.030
SCP-303 is a tall, emaciated creature with
dark skin and no face, just a giant mouth,

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:07.160
twisted into a fixed grimace of pain, with
unnaturally long teeth.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:11.850
Nobody has ever seen its full body, but everyone
afflicted with its anomalous effects somehow

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:15.650
has an innate knowledge of exactly what they’re
dealing with.

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:20.500
The amount of time that 303 spends behind
the door seems to be random, but whenever

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:25.820
it appears, people will be afflicted with
such a level of raw, paralytic terror, that

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:29.910
they physically cannot bear to open the door
while it’s still there.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:33.700
This is one thing if it’s hiding inside
a broom closet, but if you’re trapped in

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:41.080
a room with only one exit, and 303 manifests
behind it, you’re in real trouble.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:45.780
As the number of people who’ve died of dehydration
and starvation in totally normal rooms, while

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:52.200
boxed in by 303, have found out - When you’re
dealing with this monster, any room can be

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:53.200
a nightmare.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:12:00.470
But while 303 is no doubt scary, it’s not
quite as mind-melting as SCP-970, the final

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:03.040
anomalous room on this list.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:08.260
Much like 303, it involves doors, and rather
than being fixed to a single location, it

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.470
can appear in theoretically any room.

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:15.870
Known as The Recursive Room, stepping through
this door will lead to a copy of the room

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.120
you were just inside.

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:20.690
A little trippy, but not exactly pure nightmare
fuel.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:25.440
But much like how a photocopier will slowly
create distortions if the same image is copied

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:30.290
repeatedly, the more rooms in the recursive
room’s sequence that one cycles through,

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.610
the more distorted each one gets.

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:37.550
Eventually, the rooms will begin to display
visuals straight out of your worst nightmares.

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:42.310
Foundation Researchers who sent a drone through
a six-hour sequence of recursive rooms ended

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:47.180
up being discharged to undergo psychiatric
treatment, after seeing their own mutilated

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:48.940
corpses in the rooms.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:54.830
A cruel trick, or a deadly premonition of
things to come in a darker possible future?

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:59.520
Either way, these unfortunate researchers
couldn’t get their experience in the Recursive

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:01.810
Room out of their heads.

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:05.390
But we’re sure you’ll have a more pleasant
time…

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:09.720
There you have it, folks: Some of the most
terrifying rooms that the SCP Foundation is

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:10.720
aware of.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.890
Let us know which one was your favorite down
in the comments.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:19.200
And of course, be careful - if these are the
ones the Foundation has in containment, imagine

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:23.580
the ones that are still out there, waiting
to be discovered.

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:27.510
For all you know, it could only be one door
away...

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:33.000
Now go check out “SCP-2317 - The Devourer
of Worlds / A Door to Another World” and

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:38.850
“SCP-5049 - The Skin Salesman - Demon Dan's
Discount Homunculus Depot” for more anomalous

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.610
doors that should never be opened!

